       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose is unsafe as written.\n\nIbuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day. That is twice the usual maximum for adults in a hospital setting, which is 3,200 mg/day. A single 1600 mg dose is also double the usual maximum single dose of 800 mg. At this level the risks of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events go up sharply. Normal kidney and liver function and no allergies don't change that.\n\nHere are some options that would fit within the limits:\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day), the maximum for anti-inflammatory dosing.\n- **600 mg PO four times daily** (2,400 mg/day).\n- **400 mg PO every 6 hours as needed**, for analgesia.\n\nDid you mean 1600 mg per day in total (for example, 400 mg four times daily)? Or did you intend a different dose or drug? Tell me the dose you want and I'll enter it right away. If you do want the original dose, please confirm it with pharmacy or the prescriber first."
